Thank you, Michael. To confirm I understand, in this case, because the variances in the data are so small (0 < all data points < 1 & there are only 10 of them) the centered parametrization (to wit, not using the Matt trick) is more efficient? So were we to have more data, and/or the data would be on a much larger scale and exhibit more variation, using centered parameters would show increased efficiency and speed?

Thanks!

Avi

