My R package glmer2stan will translate your lmer formula to a basic, didactic Stan model. It's on github. See links here: http://xcelab.net/rm/?page_id=56

Note that I'm not actively developing glmer2stan anymore. But it will certainly work for the instructional purpose you need it for. Indeed, that's the primary reason I wrote it. See examples in the help page ?glmer2stan, after you install the package.

Also, the github Readme has several examples worked through: https://github.com/rmcelreath/glmer2stan

